An operand keeps its 64 bits. If one of the operands is negative, an
integer of 2^63 or more thus counts as the negative number with the same
bits. A double out of the 64 bit range wraps modulo 2^64, and an infinite
double counts as 0.

-- Expect stdout --
-1 & 0x8000000000000000 = -9223372036854775808
-1 | 0x8000000000000000 = -1
-1 ^ 0xffffffffffffffff = 0
-2 & 0xffffffffffffffff = -2
0x8000000000000000 & 0x8000000000000001 = 9223372036854775808
-1 & 1e19 = -8446744073709551616
-1e19 | 0 = 8446744073709551616
1e20 & 0xffffffff = 1661992960
Infinity | 0 = 0
-- End --

-- Testcase --
